  <title id="bdl08linvsnonlin-title">One Laplace posterior under the linearized and the nonlinear predictive</title>
  <desc id="bdl08linvsnonlin-desc">Two panels share a one-dimensional regression data set with inputs between 0 and 1.5 and between 2.5 and 5.8, and the same ten parameter draws from a full Laplace posterior of a small tanh network. Panel a, linearized network: the thin sample paths, the solid predictive mean and the dashed 95 percent bounds follow the data closely and widen only away from it. Panel b, nonlinear network: the sample paths swing far outside the plotted range, the dashed bounds lie outside the plot over the whole input range and the solid Monte Carlo mean misses the data.</desc>
